fof_version: '1.0'
type: enemy
id: bought_captain
name: Captain-under-Contract
ruleset:
  modules:
  - id: base
    version: 1.0.0
enemy:
  # v0.3: Boss, durability 5, attack +3, heavy armor, two specials (the Second Clause, Reform the Line), rating 15.
  level: 4
  role: boss
  armor: 2
  morale: 9
  weapon: A very good sword it would rather not draw
  wants: The fee, the company intact, and the reputation that gets the next contract.
  special: THE SECOND CLAUSE — once per fight, in the exchange after the party looks like
    winning, the captain invokes the clause only it has read, and the company's objective
    changes mid-scene in a direction the party did not plan for.
  when_bloodied: It starts negotiating out loud, mid-exchange, while the attacks continue.
    Anyone who answers is talking to someone genuinely listening. If the fight is going long,
    do this on its second exchange on the field instead of waiting.
  tells: It spends the opening exchange placing Blades and watching who the party protects.
    The contract case is chained to its belt.
  breaks: Calls the withdrawal and means it. A captain who has called a withdrawal will not
    resume the fight tonight for any inducement, including a better offer.
  twists:
  - The Second Clause is to take the party alive and deliver them to the employer.
  - The Second Clause voids the contract if the employer lied, and the employer lied.
  - A better offer, made in front of the sergeants, ends this before it starts.
  - Half the company are Blades the party has already beaten once, and they remember.
  - The captain is still hurt from the last engagement and wants this to be short.
  - The employer has come onto the field, and the captain would very much prefer otherwise.
  nastier: REFORM THE LINE — once per scene, and only if the company still has somewhere to
    withdraw to, every Blade that disengaged this scene returns to the field in good order.
  description: >-
    A captain of the Bought is a businessperson who has been shot at, and it shows in both
    directions. The coat is very good. The scar is older than the coat. The contract case
    is chained to the belt, and the chain has been replaced more recently than the case.
  notes: >-
    Level 4 Boss, armor 2: no overrides. Reform the Line moved to NASTIER so the card has
    one gimmick.


    Runs the fight the way a foreman runs a site: no heroics, no waste, and a very clear idea
    of when to stop. It never commits recklessly; it is not that kind of company. It shifts
    for a better-paying, better-terms offer made in front of the sergeants, and honours a
    bought-out contract absolutely; it is the only asset the Bought actually sell.


    Its bloodied phase keeps the v0.3 lesson (Series 13): a Boss's second act is keyed to
    conduct when the fight is long and to damage only when it is short.


    Appears: one per company of sixteen Blades and four sergeants.
  reskin_of: null
